## send feature

[X] make it so fx pads don't select in bw
    [X] use internal selection instead
[X] create a send banks for each track
[X] TwisterTrackCtl
    [X] when in send mode
        [X] disable vol / pan ring
        [X] paint corresponding send value to ring
        [X] turning encoder should set send value
        [X] will need to break TwisterTrackCtl into more responsibilities
            [X] TwisterVolPanCtl
            [X] TwisterSendTracksToFxCtl
            ->  pulling this out unlocks the pattern where one class
                controls all the encoders and knows how to activate or
                de-activate itself depending on the events that happen in
                the system
            ->  this lays the pattern for:
            [X] TwisterSendTrackToAllFxCtl
                [X] top 8 encoders control FX track volumes / pans
                    (re-use VolPan mode selector + patterns from TwisterTrackCtl)
                [X] bottom 8 encoders send selected track to all 8 FX
                -> this program gets activated after selecting a track, then
                   an FX. this is in contrast to selecting an FX when you
                   just selected a group, which activates
                   TwisterSendTracksToFxCtl instead.
[X] solo behavior
    [X] TwisterVolPanCtl
        [X] encoder button hold should solo the corresponding track
        [X] release should unsolo
        [X] set the LED to yellow when track is soloed (mirror trackctl in solo mode)
    [X] launchpad: make the solo mode selector button yellow
    [X] TwisterSendTrackToAllFxCtl
        [X] bottom encoder buttons should solo corresponding FX
        [X] top encoder buttons should solo the FX tracks they represent
    [X] TwisterSendTracksToFxCtl
        [X] all encoder buttons should solo currently selected FX track
